@page "/Error"

@*
    Target of app.UseExceptionHandler("/Error") in Program.cs, which is only
    active outside Development - i.e. in the Docker image. Without this page an
    unhandled exception fell through to the NotFound block in Routes.razor and
    rendered "nothing at this address", presenting a 500 as a 404.
    Deliberately static: no HttpContext or request-id plumbing, since under
    interactive routing HttpContext is null once the circuit starts.
*@

<PageTitle>Error - Star Trek SQL Assistant</PageTitle>

<div class="error-page">
    <h1>Something went wrong</h1>
    <p>
        The server hit an unexpected error while handling that request. This is a
        problem in the app, not with your question.
    </p>
    <p class="error-page-hint">
        The details are in the server log: <code>docker compose logs blazor-app</code>
    </p>
    <a class="error-page-home" href="/">Back to the assistant</a>
</div>
